provide for the printing, recording, broadcasting, publication and distribution ofteaching material, research reports, papers and other works which may be issuedby the Institute;establish a grievance redressal mechanism in such a manner as may beprescribed by Regulations; anddo all other acts, whether incidental to the powers aforementioned or not, as maybe requisite in order to further the objectives of the Institute as a knowledgehouse and place of education, leaming, research and service to community.
5. s ic o .-{1) The jurisdiction of the Institute shall extend to the whole of Pakistan.(2) The principal seat of the Institute shall be at Prem Nagar [slam Kot, DistrictTharparkar, Sindh.6. stitu o en to at .{1) Subject to the reasonable restictions as may be prescribed,the Institute shall be open to all persons and admission to the Institute shall not be denied on thebasis of gender, nationality, religion , race, creed, colour or domicile.
@ The Institute shall institute financial aid programmes for students in need, tothe extent considered feasible by the Board of Governors given the resources available, so asto enable admission and access to the Institute and the various opportunities provided by it tobe based on merit rather than ability to pay: Provided that the Institute may institute self-finance schemes not covering more than ten percent of the total number of candidates in anyon campus taught course or research-based programme of sfudy.
7. eac i g at t e stit te.{l) All recognized teaching in various courses shall beconducted by the lnstitute or the colleges in the prescribed manner and may includelectures, futorials, discussions, seminars, demonstrations, distance learning and othermethods of insfuction as well as practical work in the laboratories, hospitals, workshops andother govemmental or private organizations.(2) The authority responsible for organizing recognized teaching shall be such asmay be prescribed.
C-CSHS
8. cers of t e stit te.- The following shall be the Officers of the
Institute:
(a) Patron in Chief;(b) Rector;(c) Director General;(d) Deputy Director General;(e) Deans;(0 Chairpersons;(g) Registrar;(h) Treasurer;(i) Controller of Examinations;(a) Director, Quality Enhancement Cell;C) Director, Office of Research, Irurovation and Commercialization;ft) Librarian; and(l) such other persons as may be prescribed by Regulations to be the officersof the Institute.Page 5 of 23

