g. atro i C ief.-{l) The Patron in Chief or his nominee shall preside over aconvocation of the Institute.
(2) The Institute may confer an honorary degree with the prior approval of thePatron in Chief.
10. s ectio a n i .-{1) The Patron in Chief may cause inspection orinquiry into the affairs of the Institute.(2) The Patron in Chief shall convey his views with regard to the result ofinspection or inquiry to the Board and may, after ascertaining the views of the Board,recommend any remedial action to the Board.
(3) The Board shall, within the time specified by the Patron in Chief submit areport to the Patron in Chief about the action taken on the recommendations of the Patronin Chief.
(4) If the Board fails to take action to the satisfaction of the Patron in Chief withinthe specified time, the Paton in Chief may issue such directions as he thinks fit and theBoard shall comply with all such directions.
Provided that no action under subsection (4) shall be taken unless the Rector of theBoard is afforded an opportunity of being heard.11. ector.{l) The Rector of the Board shall be appointed by the Board of Directors fora renewable period of four (04) years, as the Board of Directors may determine.
(2) The Rector shall, preside over the meetings of the Board.
12. e oval o the oar of Gover ors.{l) The Rector may, upon the recommendationof the Review Panel, remove any person from the mernbership of the Board of Governors on theground that such person:(a) has become of unsound mind; or(b) has become incapacitated to function as member of the Board ofGovernors; or(c) has been convicted by a court of law for an offence involvingmoral turpitude: or(d) has absented himself from two consecutive meetings without justcause; or(e) has been guilty of misconduct, including use of position forpersonal advantage of any kind, or gross inefficiency in theperformance of functions.
(2) 'the Rector shall remove any person from the membership of the Board of Governorson a resolution calling for the removal of such person supported by at least three-fourths ofthe membership of the Board of Governors:
Provided that before passing such resolution the Board of Governors shall provide themember concemed a fair hearing.
13. irector e era.-{l) The Board of Directors of the Trust shall, on thePage 6 of 23

