recommendations of the Board, appoint a person as Director General.(2) The Board shall constitute a Searoh Committee for making recommendations for theappoi ent of Director General.(3) The Board shall determine the terms and conditions of service of the DirectorGeneral.( ) The irector General shall be the person who possesses the prescribed qualificationsand experience.(5) The Director General shall perform such functions as are given in the Act or as maybe prescribed or assigned to him by the Board.
I . owers a d ties of t e irector e eral.{l) The Director General shall be thechief executive officer of the Institute responsible for all administrative and academic functionsof the Institute and for ensuring that the provisions of the Ac! Rules and Regulations areobserved in all affairs of the Institute.
(2) The Director General may attend a meeting of any Authority or body of the Institute.(3) The Director General may, in an emergency thatin his opinion requires immediateaction ordinarily not in the competence of the Director General, take such action andforward, within seventy-two hours, a report of the action taken to the members of theEmergency Committee of the Board of Governors, to be set up by Statute, TheEmergency Committee may direct such further action as is considered appropriate.
(4\ The Subject to the general supervision and control of the Board, the DirectorGeneral may:
a)
b)c)d)e)0s)h)
direct a teacher, offtcer or other employee of the Instifute to take up suchassignment in connection with examination, administration or any otheractivities in the Institute as he may consider necessary;sanction by re-appropriation an amount for an unforeseen item not providedfor in the budget of the Institute;make appointments of such categories of employees of the Institute and insuoh manner as may be prescribed by Regulations;suspend, punish or remove, in the prescribed manner, an officer, teacher oremployee of the Institute except those appointed by the Board;take disciplinary action against a teacher, officer or any other employee ofthe Institute in the prescribed manner;relax Regulations in favour of a student in a case of real hardship and reportthe action to the Board in its immediate next meeting;delegate, subject to such conditions as may be prescribe4 any of his powersto a teacher or officer of the Institute; andexercise such other powers as may be prescribed or as may be assigned tohim by the Board from time to time.
(5) The Director General shall prepare an annual report containing information asregards the preceding academic yeff including disclosure of all relevant facts pertainingto academics, research, administration and finances of the Instifute for the information ofthe Board.
(6) The Director General shall, within three months of the conclusion of anacademic year, submit the annual report of the Institute to the Board.15. e ty irector e eral.{l) There shall be a Deputy Director General ofthe Institute to be appointed by the Board on such terms and conditions as the Board mayPageT of 23

