(3) The Chairperson shall plan, organize and supervise the work of a teaching orresearch department, constituent college or constituent institute, as the case may be, and shallbe responsible to the Dean for the work assigned to him.. egistrar.-(1) The Board shall appoint a Registrar of the Institute.(2) The experience, professional and academic qualifications necessary for appointmentto the post of Registrar, method and manner of appoinftnent as well as terms and conditionsof appointment shall be as may be prescribed by Regulations.(3) The Board shall not appoint a person as Regishar unless he possesses theprescribed qualifications and experience and other requirements of the post.(4) The Registrar shall be a full time officer ofthe Institute and shall:a) be the administrative head of the secretariat of the Institute and beresponsible for the provision of secretarial support to the Board and theDirector General;b) be the custodian of the common seal and the academic records of theInstitute;c) maintain a register of the students and graduates in the prescribed manner;d) prepare and update the Handbook of Rules and Regulations approved byAuthorities, bodies or committees from time to time, and make themavailable to public, all respective members of the Authorities and Officers ofthe Institute;e) enticate records on behalf of the Institute0 supervise the process of appointment or nomination of a member to anAuthority or body of the Institute in the prescribed manner; andg) perform such other duties as may be prescribed or as may be assigned to himby the Director General or the Board from time to time'(5) When the office of the Registrar is vacant or the Registrar is absent or unable toperform his functions owing to any cause, the Board shall make temporary arrangementsfor the performance ofthe duties of Registrar.. Co tro er of xa i atio s.-(l) The Board shall appoint a Controller ofExaminations of the Institute.
(2) The experience, professional and academic qualifications necessary forappointment to the post of Controller of Examinations, method and manner ofappointment as well as terms and conditions of appointment shall be as may beprescribed by Regulations.(3) The Board shall not appoint a person as Controller of Examinations unless hepossesses the prescribed qualifications and experience and other requirements of the post.(4) The Confroller of Examinations shall be a full-time officer of the Institute andshali 'be responsible for all matters connected with the conduct of examinations,maintenance -of evaluation and assessment records, and perform such other duties as maybe prescribed or assigned to him by the Director General or the Board from time to time.(5) When the office of the Confroller of Examinations is vacant or the Controllerof dxaminations is absent or unable to perform his functions owing to any cause, the
