2 . oar of over ors.{l) The Board of Governors of the Institute shallconsist of the following:(a) A Director-of the Trust, to be nominated by the BoD, shall be the Rector of theBoard;Oi Directors of the Trust subject to a maximum of six Directors to be nominatedby the Trust;(c) Two persons from professionals of different fields each one of whom is an.*p.rt in any of the fields of kn-owledge to be nominated by the Rector of the Board;(d) Secretary to the Governmenq Federal Education Department or his nominee;Gi Rector of the Intemational Islatnic Institute or his nominee;ift A Director General of a Federal Inst of Pakistan to be nominated by thePatron in Chief;(g) Rector of the Institute;(h) Deputy Director General ofthe lnstitute; and(i) Registrar (Secretary).(2) Members of the Board other than ex-fficio members shall hold office for a term ofihr", y"*, and shall be eligible for re appoi ent on the expiry of their term of office.(3) The quorum for a meiting of the-Board shall be one half of the total number ofmembers with at least two ex-fficio members, a fiaction being counted as one'(4) The Secretary shai[, with the approval of the Rector of the Board, call ameeting of the Board.(5) In the absence of Rector of the Board, the Deputy Rector of the Board shallpr6iO. at the meetings of the Board and perform all the functions and powers of theRector.
(6) e Board shall meet at least once in a calendar year'(7)Unless otherwise prescribed by this Act, all decisions of the Board shall be taken ontt e Uuris of the opinion ff majority bf m" members present. In the event of the membersbeing evenly dividid on any matter, the Rector of the Board shall have a casting vote.Page 1 of23

