(S)The Trust may fill a casual vacancy occurring because of death or resignation of amember of the Board nominated by the Trust to the extent of the remainder of the term of theformer member.
25. owers a uties of t e oar .{1) The administration and managementof the affairs of the Institute shall vest in the Board. The Board shall have the power ofgeneral supervision over the Institute and shall hold the Offrcers and Authorities of theInstitute accountable for all the functions of the Institute.
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers, the Board o1'Governors shall have the following powers:-(a) to approve the proposed annual plan ofwork, the annual and revised budgets,the annual report and the annual statement of account;(b) to hotd, control and lay down policy for the administration of the property,funds and investments of the lnstitute, including the approval of the sale andpurchase or acquisition of immovable property;(c) to oversee the quality and relevance of the Institute's academic programmesand to review the academic affairs of the Institute in general;(d) to approve the appointment of the Deans, Professors, Associate Professors andsuch other senior faculty and senior administrators as may be prescribed;(e) to institute schemes, directions and guidelines for the terms and conditions ofappointment of all officers, teachers and other employees of the Institute;(f) to approve strategic plans;(g) to invest any money belonging to the Institute.(h) to approve financial resource development plans of the Institute;(i) to consider the drafts of Statutes and Regulations proposed by the ExecutiveCommittee and the Academic Council and deal with them in the manner asprovided for in sections 27 and 30, as the case may be:
Provided that the Board of Governors may frame a Statute with respect to any matter irits power or with respect after calling for the advice of the Executive Committee as the case;may be.
(a) to annul by order in writing the proceedings of any Authority or officer if tht:Board of Govemors is satisfied that such proceedings are not in accordancewith the provisions of the Act, Statutes or Regulations after calling upon suchAuthority or officer to show cause why such proceedings should not b,lannulled;(b) to recommend to the Rector removal of any member of the Board ofGovernors in accordance with the provisions of the Act;(c) to make appointment of members of the Executive Committee, other than ex-officio members, in accordance with the provisions of the Act;(d) to make appointment of members of the Academic Council, other than e>lofficio members, in accordance with the provisions of the Act;(e) to appoint Emeritus Professors on such terms and conditions as may treprescribed;(f) to remove any person from the membership of any Authority if such person:i. has become of unsound mind; orii. has become incapacitated to function as member of suc;hAuthority; oriii. has been convicted by a court of law for an offence involvingmoral turpitude; and(g) to determine the form, provide for the custody and regulate the use of thecommon seal ofthe Institute.Page 12 of il3

endstream
