(3) e Board may, subject to the provisions of this Ac! delegate all or any of itspowers and functions to any Authority, Committee or OfEcer except the following:a) approval of Regulations;b) recommend any action to the Patron in Chief;ci appoinfinent of Registrar, Confoller of Examination and Treasurer; andd) approval of annual budget and consideration of audit rcports.
26. B si ess o t e oar .{1) The meetings and business of the Board shall beconducted in such manner and in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed inRegulations and until so prescribed, as may be determined by the Board.(2) The Regulation or proceeding of the Board shall not be invalid by reason of anyvacancy or defect in the constitution of the Board.7, e xec tive o ittee.{l) There shall be an Executive Committee ofthe Institute consisting of the following:-(a) the Director General; who shall be its Chairperson;O) the DePutY Director Generals;(c) the Deans of the Faculties of the Institute;(d) three professors from different dep ents;(e) Directors of the constitueirt colleges;(D Principals of the constituent colleges/institutions;(g) the Registrar; who shall be its Secretary;O) the Treasurer; and(D the Controller of Examinations.
(2) Members of the Executive Committee, other than ex-officio members, shall holdoffice for three years.(3) The quonrm for a meeting of the Executive Committee shall be one half of the totalnumber of members, a fraction being counted as one.(a) The Executive Committee shall meet at least once in each quarter ofthe year.
28. owers a uties of t e Exec tive o ittee.{l) The Executive Committeeshall be the executive body of the Institute and shall, subject to the provisions of the Act andthe Statute, exercise gene.al supervision ever the affairs and management of the Institute.(a) without prejudice to the generality of foregoing powers, and to theprovisionr oi the Act, the statute and ctions of the Board of rs' theExecutive Committee shall have the following powers:(b) to consider the annual report, the annual and revised budget estimates and tosubmit these to the Board of Governors;(c) to transfer and accept transfer of movable properly on behalf of the Institute;(d) to enter into, yary, carry out and cancel contracts on behalf of the Institute;(e) to cause proper books of account to be kept for all sums of money received andPage Lt of 23

