(4) The Representation Committee for appointments to the Executive Committee and theAcademic Council shall consist ofthe following:(a) two members of the Board of Govemors who are not Institute Teachers;fu) tt r"" persons nominated by the Institute Teachers from amongst themselves in themanner prescribed;
(5) The tenure of the Representation Committees shall be three years: Provided that nomember shall serve for more than two consecutiveterms.(6) The procedures of the Representation Committees shall be as may be prescribed.(7) There may also be such other Representation Committees set up by any of the otherAuthoiities of the Institute as are considered appropriate for recommending persons forappoi ent to the various Authorities and other bodies of the Institute.3. ca e ic o cil.{l)TheAcademiccouncilshallconsistof:a) Rector (Convener);b) Deputy Director General;c) all Deans;dj Principals and Directors of constituent colleges and constituentinstitutes;e) Director, Quality Enhancement Cell;D Director, Officeof search, Innovation and commercialization;g) Chairpersons of the academic and research departments;[j tnr." p.. , includin least on , eminent in sciences, social- sciences arts, of m one from each oategory, to benominated by the Rector of the Board;i) all Professors of the Institute;ji four Institute teachers, otherthan Professors, two from each category ofAssociate professors and Assistant Professors, to be appointed by theBoard;k) secretary to Government, Higher Education Department or hisnominee;l) Director Academics of the Commission;m) Controller of Examinations;n) Librarian; ando) Registrar (Member/Secretary).(Z) embers of the Academic Council other than ex-officio members shall hold office for aterm of ee years and shall be eligible for re-appointment on the expiry of theirterm of office.(3) The quorum for a meeting of the Academic Council shall be one-third of the totalnumber'of membirs with at least two ex-officio members, a fraction being counted as one'(4) The Academic council shall meet at least once in six months.3 . ers a d es of ca e ic Co ncit.{l) e Academic Council shallbe the academic body of the Institute and may, subject to Regulations, lay down proper standards ofPage 15 of 23

