instruction, research, publication and examination and regulate and promote the academic life of thr:
Institute.
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers and subject to theprovisions of the Act, Rules and Regulations, the Academic Council may:(a) advise the Board on academic matters;(b) regulate the conduct ofteaching, research and publication;(c) regulate the admission of students to the courses of study and examinations in ttteInstitute;( ) regulate the award of studentships, scholarships, exhibitions, medals and prizes;(e) regulate the conduct and discipline of the students of the Institute;(f) propose to the Board, schemes for the constitution and organization of faculties,teaching departments, constituent colleges, constituent instifutes and otheracademic bodies;(g) recommend policies and procedures pertaining to the quality of academicprograms to the Board;( ) consider or formulate proposals for the planning and development of teaching a;rdresearch in the Institute;(i) recommend to the Board, the Regulations prescribing the courses of studies, thesyllabi and outlines of tests for examinations;fi) recognize the examinations of other universities or examining bodies as equivalentto the corresponding examinations of the Institute;( frame Regulations for submission to the Board;(l) institute programs for the continuous professional development of Instit'uteteachers at all levels;( )prepare an annual report on the academic performance of the Institute for theinformation of Board;(n) appoint or nominate members to various Authorities in accordanoe with theprovisions of the Act; and(o) perform such other functions as may be prescribed by Regulations or assigned bythe Board.
32. ac lties.{l) There shall be a Faculty or a group of Faculties for a teachingdepartment or a group of teaching departments as may be prescribed by the Act, Rule,s orRegulations.
33. oar of acul .-{1) There shall be a Board of Faculty for each Facultywhich shall consist of:(a) Dean ofthe Faculty (Convener);(b) Professors and the Chairpersons in the Faculty;(c) two teachers to be nominated by the Academic Council on the basis oftheir specialized knowledge of the subjects which, though not assigne,d tothe Faculty, have in the opinion of the Academic Council, impo;r'tantbearing on the subjects assigned to the Faculty;(d) two experts, in the field from outside the Institute to be appointed by thsBoard; and(e) one member from amongst the Officers of the Institute to be nominated bythe Director General.
(2) The members other than ex-officio members of a Board of Faculty shall holdoffice for a term of three years and shall be eligible for re-appointment on the expiry oftheir term of office.
