(2) Each Board of Studies shall consist of:(a) the Chairperson of the teaching department (Convener);(b) all the teachers of the teaching department; and(c) a maximum of three experts or teachers, other than lnstitute teachers, tcrbe appointed by the Director General according to the need of each Boarclof Studies.
(3) The members other than ex officio members of the Board of Studies shall holdoffice for a term of three years and shall be eligible for re-appointment on the expiry oftheir term of office.
(4) The quorum for a meeting of the Board of Studies shall be one-half the totalnumber of members, a fraction being counted as one.
37. nctio s of oar s of St ies.-A Board of Studies shall perform thefollowing functions:(a) advise the Authorities on all academic matters connected with instructiorr,publication, research and examination in the subject or subjects concerned;(b) propose curricula and syllabi for all degree, diploma and certifrcate coursesin the subject or subjects concemed;(c) suggest a panel of names of paper setters and examiners in the subject orsubjects concemed; and(d) undertake such other functions as may be prescribed by Regulations.
38. eac i g e art e ts.{l) There shall be a Teaching Department or ;mInstitute for each subject or a group of subjects, as may be prescribed by Regulations aradeach Teaching Department or an Institute shall, as the case may be, headed by theChairperson.
39. Selectio oard.-(l) The Selection Board shall consist of:
a. Rector; (Convener);b. Dean ofthe Faculty concerned;c. Chairperson concerned;d. Two experts in the subject to be nominated by the DirectorGeneral;e. One eminent scholar to be nominated by the Trust; andf. Registrar(Secretary).(2) The members other than ex-officio members of the Selection Board shall holdoffice for a term of three years and shall be eligible for re appointment on the expiry oftheir term of office.(3) Four members of the Selection Board shall constitute the quorum for ameeting of the Selection Board.(a) No member who is a candidate or whose family member is a candidate, fcrr apost to which appointrnent is to be made, shall take part in the proceedings of theSelection Board for selection of a candidate on such post.(5) In selection of candidates for the post of Professor or Associate Professor, theSelection Board shall co-opt or consult three experts in the subject concerned and inselecting candidates for any other teaching post two experts in the subject concerned, tobe nominated by the Director General from a standing list of experts for each sub.iectapproved by the Board on the recommendation of the Selection Board.(6) The Board may revise the standing list of experts of a subject on therecommendation of the Selection Board.Page 18 of 23

