(a) consider the applications and recommend to the Board, the names ofsuitable candidates for appoi ent to teaching and other posts andrecommend suitable salary for the selected candidate;(b) consider all cases of promotion of oflicers ofthe Institute and recommendthe names of suitable candidates for such promotion to the Board; and(c) consider all cases of honorari4 allowances, incentives for teaching andother posts and submit specific recommendations to the Board for itsconsideration.. i a ce a a i co ittee.{l) The Finance and PlanningCommittee shall consist of:(a) Rector (Convener);(b) All the Deans;(c) One nominee of the Trust;(d) One member of the Board to be nominated by the Board;(e) Director Planning of the Commission;(fj Oirector, Office of Research, Innovation and Commercialization;(g) Registrar; and(h) Treasurer (Secretary)(2) The members other than ex-officio members of the Finance and PlanningCommittee shall hold office for a term of three years and shall be eligible for reappointment on the expiry of their term of office.(3) Four members of the Finance and Planning Committee shall constitute the quorumfor a meeting ofthe Finance and Planning Committee'2, ctiosofte iacea anigco iee.-TheFinanceandPlanning Committee shall:(a) prepare the annual statement of accounts and propose annual budgetestimates and advise the Board thereon;(b) review periodically the furancial position of the Institute;icj advise the Board on all matters relating to fee structure, finance, investmentsand accounts ofthe Institute; and(d) perform such other functions as may be prescribed by the Regulations.3. isci i e Co ittee.{l) The Discipline Committee shall consist ofi(a) the Convener to be nominated by the Director General;(b) two Professors to be nominated by the Board;(c) two Associate Professors to be nominated by the Academic Council; andial tfr" teacher or officer-in-charge of students' affairs, by whatever name called(Member/Secretary).(2) The members other than ex-officio members of the Discipline Committee shall holdoffice for a term of three years and shall be eligible for re-appointment on the expiry of their termof offrce.
(3) The quorum for a meeting of the Discipline Committee shall be four members'
