51. les.{l) e Authorities and the other bodies of the Institutemay make Rules, to be published in the Institute's Gazette, consistent with the Act Statutesor the Regulations, to regulate any matter relating to the affairs of the lnstitute which has notbeen provided for by the Act or that is not required to be regulated by Statutes or Regulations,including rules to regulate the conduct of business and the time and place of meetings andrelated matters.
(2) Rules shall become effective upon approval by the Board of
Governors.
