benefit of its officers, teachers and other employees schemes, as may be prescribed, for theprovision of post employment benefits as well as health and life insurance while in service.55. e ova o i c lties. --(1) If any question arises as to theinterpretation of any of the provisions of the Act, it shall be placed before the Patron in Chiefand Higher, Education Commission (I{EC) whose decision thereon shall be final.(2) lf any difficulty arises in giving effect to any of the provisions of the Act,the Patron in Chief may make such order after obtaining the views of the Board ofGovemors, not inconsistent with the provisions of the Ac! as may appear to him to benecessary for removing the difficulty.(3) Where the Act makes any provision for anything to be done but no provisionor no sufficient provision has been made as respects the authority by whom, or the time atwhich, or the manner in which, it shall be done, then it shall be done by such authority, atsuch time, or in such manner as the Paton in Chief may direct after obtaining the views ofthe Board ofGovernors.
56. e ni .-No suit or legal proceedings shall lie against the Instituteor any Authority, officer or employee of the Institute or any person in respect of anythingwhich is done in good faith under the Act.SA N S AS Se purpose and objects of the establishment of The Thar International Institute, is topromote and disseminate the knowledge and to provide education, training, research,demonstration and scholarship in such branches of learning, as it may determine in Thar andother backward areas of the country. For this purpose, the application and advancement aswell as dissemination of knowledge in field of Computer Sciences and IT including AI,Liberal Arts, Social Sciences and Business & Public Administration. To determine coursesfor study at the under graduate and higher levels in its constituents units and institutions shallbe obtained and liaison with other research or academic organizations shall be made toachieve the targets. Further, Industry and the relevant organizations or institutions to promotepublic private partnership, innovation and research, developmen! indusffialization for thepurpose of education, training development shall be made. This Bill seeks to achieve theaforesaid objectives.
